# Percentage comparison against a plain value rejected

Verifies a comparison between a qualified percentage and a plain number is rejected at compile time. An unannotated 25% literal carries the percentage subtype with no compatible rule for plain integers, so the compiler reports the undefined operand pair instead of dropping the qualification.

>>> source
print(25% == 25)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: comparison `==` is not defined for `int64[%]` and `int64` at Span { start: 6, end: 15 }

<<< exit
1
